# Data Quality Assessment

## 1. Dataset Overview

This project uses the Repeat Buyer E-commerce Dataset published on Mendeley Data.

- **Dataset:** Repeat Buyer E-commerce Dataset
- **Source:** [Mendeley Data](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hwvz4kv232/1)
- **Total Records:** 1,000 rows
- **Total Columns:** 10
- **Observation Period:** June 1, 2022 – July 31, 2022

## 2. Data Quality Checks

The initial assessment was conducted to identify missing values, duplicate records, inconsistent data types, and potential data inconsistencies.

| Quality Check | Result |
|---|---|
| Total records | 1,000 |
| Total columns | 10 |
| Missing values | 0 |
| Exact duplicate rows | 0 |
| Date conversion | Converted to datetime |
| Invalid dates after conversion | 0 |

## 3. Data Cleaning

The following preparation steps were performed:

- Converted `Trx_Date` from text into datetime format using the month/day/year convention.
- Standardized the `Category` value for Product_ID `121314151` from `E` to `Body Treatment`, based on the other records associated with the same product.
- Verified the data types of `Age` and `Amount`.
- Retained all 1,000 records during the initial cleaning process.

## 4. Data Quality Notes and Limitations

Several points require further investigation before advanced analysis:

- The meaning and measurement unit of `Amount` have not yet been confirmed from the dataset documentation. Therefore, it will not be interpreted as revenue or quantity until verified.
- Some product names may contain inconsistent formatting and require further review.
- The dataset does not contain an explicit order ID. Consequently, repeated customer records cannot automatically be interpreted as distinct orders.
- The dataset covers only two months, which limits the interpretation of long-term customer retention and cohort behavior.

## 5. Conclusion

The initial data preparation identified no missing values or exact duplicate records. Date formatting was standardized, and one inconsistent product category value was corrected.

Further validation of business definitions and dataset limitations will be considered before conducting customer behavior and retention analysis.
